# Test-run protocol vocabulary (PT-9): the words TestRunProtocol.cs's Lifecycle/RunOutcome/LeafOutcome/Health
# string-const classes and testing.py's _RUN_STATES/_TERMINAL_OUTCOMES duplicate by hand. One ENUM per word
# set, printed to both languages by `data --target cs|py`. TerminalOutcome records which RunOutcome values are
# failures (isFailure), giving the required RECORD real protocol content instead of filler.
ENUM Lifecycle prepared|dispatched|running|finalizing|terminal
ENUM RunOutcome passed|failed|cancelled|incomplete|invalid|dispatch_failed
ENUM LeafOutcome passed|failed|skipped|inconclusive|cancelled|invalid
ENUM Health healthy|reloading|no_test_progress|editor_unresponsive|suspected_stall
ENUM EventType run_started|manifest_sealed|test_started|test_finished|run_finished|infrastructure_error|dispatch_failed|cancel_requested|abandoned|cancelled|domain_reloading|run_finalized

RECORD TerminalOutcome KEY outcome COUNT 6
  outcome: string
  isFailure: bool
END
